  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "4",
  "quote": "a provision in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with this Act or the regulations is void",
  "reason": "Section 119 of the Act permits a landlord to increase the rent after at least 12 months have elapsed since the day the unit was first rented to the tenant. Because this clause restricts a statutory right provided to the landlord by the Act, it is inconsistent with the Act and therefore void under subsection 4(1)."
}

